{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.25,
    "explanation": "The SGD 6.00 no-show fee is placed on hold: this dispute goes to a human reviewer and no money is collected or refunded in the meantime. That is not a finding for either of you — it is the honest result when the record cannot show what actually happened at the kerb.\n\nWhat is not in dispute, [Driver], is the shape of the trip: your arrived marker is at 23:42:10 and you cancelled at 23:49:05, an interval of 415 seconds, and the reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW is one POL-NS-01(d) recognises. [Rider], your account is corroborated to this extent: the driver's own GPS fixes put the car inside the 150 m airport arrival radius at five qualifying fixes, closing to 96 m.\n\nWhy it cannot be decided. POL-NS-01(c) requires a continuous in-geofence dwell of 480 seconds, measured from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix. The only artifact that can measure that is EV-GPS-00210, and it is impaired for policy purposes under POL-NS-08(a) and (b): its device clock runs 228 seconds ahead of the server, a 186-second sampling gap sits exactly across the moment of geofence entry, coverage is 22.8%, the trace stops 149 seconds before the cancellation, and it carries no rider track. Read at face value its longest continuous in-geofence run is 255 seconds; corrected for the skew the same entry point yields 632 seconds, and the gap conceals which figure is right. The trip record (EV-TRIP-00210, weight 0.4, CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT) says 6.9 minutes but is itself impaired and cannot break the tie, and the chat log (EV-CHAT-00210, weight 0.6, TRUNCATED_LOG) is missing the messages exchanged during the wait. Because the sole deciding fact rests on a single artifact impaired under POL-NS-08(a) and (b), and because two artifacts contradict each other directly on arrival and dwell with no clause able to resolve the conflict, the case escalates under POL-NS-09(b) and (e). Confidence is capped at 0.25 by POL-GEN-02(2) — the weight of the only artifact carrying the dwell — and so also falls below the 0.70 floor in POL-NS-09(a).\n\nClaims answered. [Driver]'s POL-NS-07 claim for SGD 4.80: POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and limbs (b) and (c) cannot be established here, so no compensation issues now; the anti-farming figures you cite do not trip (2 terminations against 156 completed trips), but that check was never reached. Your POL-NS-02 proximity point (96 m, 5 qualifying fixes) is accepted, and is why POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) is not engaged — but proximity is not dwell. [Rider]'s POL-NS-06 shortfall point (255 s, or 404 s to cancellation, or 415 s on the trip record, against 480 s) is not proved on an artifact this broken, because the skew-corrected reading passes the minimum and the gap hides the entry moment; and POL-NS-04 cannot be run, because your only surviving message was sent 35 seconds after the cancellation and there is no rider track for limb (c). POL-NS-05 is unavailable because the 228-second skew makes matching the arrived marker to a fix unsafe, so no false-arrival finding is entered and no referral is made. Your POL-GEN-03 point is correct — NO_ACTION would leave the charge against you — but it is not the outcome. The fare breakdown itself is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 and the SGD 6.00 line reconciles with the AIRPORT zone-class fee, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged.\n\nFor the reviewer: the open question is when the vehicle actually entered the T1 Door 6 geofence and whether the continuous in-geofence dwell reached 480 seconds — in other words, whether the 23:42:10 arrived marker is true or false — and the complete message history for 23:42–23:49 should be recovered so the contact between the parties can be assessed."
